{
  "name": "JK-BMS (RS485 adapter / GPS port)",
  "description": "For JK-BMS (Jikong) JK-B / JK-BD boards with the JK RS485 adapter (or the GPS/UART port)\n- Wiring: JK RS485 adapter in the BMS GPS port, A/B to a USB-RS485 adapter; or GPS-port TX/RX/GND to a USB-TTL adapter.\n- Do NOT connect the GPS port's VBAT pin to the adapter.\n- 115200 baud 8N1. Modbus unit id is not used.\n- Current: positive=charge, negative=discharge.\n- The newer JK-PB inverter BMS (Modbus RS485) is a different protocol and is not covered by this profile.",
  "protocol": "jk-rs485",
  "transport": "rs232",
  "defaults": {
    "baud": 115200,
    "dataBits": 8,
    "stopBits": 1,
    "parity": "none"
  },
  "metrics": [
